.TH PHPVPN 1 "2026-10-27" "phpvpn 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phpvpn \- command line client of the phpvpn service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phpvpn
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phpvpn
controls the local
.BR phpvpn-service (8)
over its public control socket
.IR /run/phpvpn/control-v1.sock .
It is a pure IPC client: it never creates the tunnel interface and never reads
or writes the configuration file itself, so it needs neither root nor a
graphical session. Installing, starting and stopping the service are not IPC
operations; use
.BR systemctl (1)
for them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the current service and connection state as JSON.
.TP
.B connect
Ask the service to establish the connection.
.TP
.B disconnect
Ask the service to stop the connection.
.TP
.B info
Print the verified server information exactly as the service returns it.
.TP
.B get-config
Print the stored configuration document exactly as stored.
.TP
.BI set-config " file"
Store the configuration document read from
.IR file .
The service validates it and publishes it atomically. Documents larger than
512 KiB are rejected with
.BR config_too_large .
.TP
.B diagnostics
Print the extended local diagnostics snapshot as JSON.
.SH OUTPUT
Enveloped answers are printed as indented JSON on standard output.
A failure is printed on standard error as one line
.RI \(dq code : " description" \(dq,
or as the description of the local IPC error. When the service cannot be
reached, a second line starting with
.B hint:
names the likely cause (service not running, socket missing, permission).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The service rejected the command, could not be reached within 10 seconds,
or the configuration file could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/phpvpn/control-v1.sock
Control socket, mode 0666. The client only talks to a peer running as root.
.TP
.I /etc/phpvpn/config.json
Configuration, readable by root only; use
.B get-config
instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phpvpn-service (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
